{"name":"Iqaluit Ice","hex":"#93cfe3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2/B language code for Icelandic."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water in frozen (solid) form.","Any frozen volatile chemical, such as ammonia or carbon dioxide."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Iqaluit","blocks":[{"text":"Iqaluit is the capital of the Canadian territory of Nunavut. Located on Baffin Island, it is the territory's largest community and only city, and the northernmost city in Canada. It was known as Frobisher Bay from 1942 to 1987, after the large bay on the coast on which the city is situated. Its traditional Inuktitut name was restored in 1987."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Iqaluit%2C_Nunavut.jpg/330px-Iqaluit%2C_Nunavut.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iqaluit","wikidata":"Q2030"},{"title":"Ice","blocks":[{"text":"Ice is water that is frozen into a solid state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °C, 32 °F, or 273.15 K. It occurs naturally on Earth, on other planets, in Oort cloud objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a mineral. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of soil or bubbles of air, it can appear transparent or a more or less opaque bluish-white color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg/330px-Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice","wikidata":"Q23392"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Leg_Building_Iqaluit_2000-08-27.jpg/500px-Leg_Building_Iqaluit_2000-08-27.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Leg_Building_Iqaluit_2000-08-27.jpg/1280px-Leg_Building_Iqaluit_2000-08-27.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Leg_Building_Iqaluit_2000-08-27.jpg/500px-Leg_Building_Iqaluit_2000-08-27.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeg_Building_Iqaluit_2000-08-27.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Iqaluit_St._Jude%27s_Anglican_Cathedral_2012.JPG/500px-Iqaluit_St._Jude%27s_Anglican_Cathedral_2012.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Iqaluit_St._Jude%27s_Anglican_Cathedral_2012.JPG/1280px-Iqaluit_St._Jude%27s_Anglican_Cathedral_2012.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Iqaluit_St._Jude%27s_Anglican_Cathedral_2012.JPG/500px-Iqaluit_St._Jude%27s_Anglican_Cathedral_2012.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIqaluit_St._Jude's_Anglican_Cathedral_2012.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Iqaluit_airport_%286869460992%29.jpg/500px-Iqaluit_airport_%286869460992%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Iqaluit_airport_%286869460992%29.jpg/500px-Iqaluit_airport_%286869460992%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIqaluit_airport_(6869460992).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.o